{
  "item_id": "PRISMA_2020_3",
  "elements": [
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_3_e1",
      "status": "PRESENT",
      "chunk_id": "text_6",
      "quote": "Currently, there are only a few interventions hat seem able to benefit the clinical course of COVID-19 [3]. Therefore, preventive measures are of vital importance to control COVID-19. The scientific, medical, and industrial communities have embarked on efforts to develop safe vaccines [4, 5]. At September 13 th , 2021 about 104 vaccines are being tested in humans, with 33 having reached phase III trials [6]. Of these, five vaccines were abandoned due to either lack of response or an undesirable adverse event (e.g., tested false positive for HIV), eight have been approved for full use, and eleven have been authorized for early or limited use [6].",
      "reason": "The manuscript describes the current state of knowledge regarding COVID-19 vaccine development, including the number of vaccines in testing, phase III trials, and approval status."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_3_e2",
      "status": "PRESENT",
      "chunk_id": "text_6",
      "quote": "With the rapid development, approval of vaccines for COVID-19, and the growing number of viral variants, there is a need for systematic reviews critically appraising the topic.",
      "reason": "The authors explicitly state the need for the review due to the rapid development of vaccines and the emergence of viral variants."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_3_e3",
      "status": "PRESENT",
      "chunk_id": "text_6",
      "quote": "We recently published the first version of our review as a preprint, showing effects of mRNA and viral vector vaccines [7]. The aim of this second version of our living systematic review is to assess the effectiveness and safety of COVID-19 vaccines through analyses of all currently available randomized clinical trials.",
      "reason": "The authors identify and cite the previous version of their own review, explaining that this is an update (second version) of their living systematic review."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_3_e4",
      "status": "NOT_APPLICABLE",
      "chunk_id": null,
      "quote": null,
      "reason": "The review evaluates the effectiveness and safety of vaccines in general, rather than focusing on a specific mechanism of action for a single intervention type."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_3_e5",
      "status": "NOT_APPLICABLE",
      "chunk_id": null,
      "quote": null,
      "reason": "The review is a standard systematic review of randomized clinical trials for vaccines and does not involve complex interventions or delivery contexts requiring a logic model."
    }
  ],
  "confidence": 100
}

{
